### ===== RUN 1, 2, 3 FIRST (restart the backend before testing) =====

### 1. Login as CUSTOMER Maria
# @name mariaLogin
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "maria.santos@gmail.com",
  "password": "Customer@123"
}

### 2. Login as STAFF Marco
# @name staffLogin
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marco.delosreyes@gmail.com",
  "password": "Staff@123"
}

### 3. Register a second customer, Liza (logged in automatically)
# @name lizaRegister
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Liza Ramos",
  "email": "liza.ramos@gmail.com",
  "phone": "09061234567",
  "password": "Liza2026pass"
}

@mariaToken = {{mariaLogin.response.body.token}}
@staffToken = {{staffLogin.response.body.token}}
@lizaToken = {{lizaRegister.response.body.token}}


### ===== SLOT AVAILABILITY (public, for the time buttons) =====

### 4. Slots for Oct 10, 4 guests (expect 5 slots; 19:00 has 6 tables left, others 7)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/slots?date=2026-10-10&guests=4

### 5. Too many guests (expect 400)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/slots?date=2026-10-10&guests=11

### 6. Past date (expect 400)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/slots?date=2026-10-01&guests=2


### ===== BOOKING WITH AUTO-ASSIGNED TABLE =====

### 7. Maria books Oct 15, 7 PM, 4 guests, and TRIES to pick Table 12
###    (expect 201: Table 12 is IGNORED, she gets Table 5, the smallest that fits)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{mariaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Maria Santos",
  "customerEmail": "maria.santos@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09171234567",
  "date": "2026-10-15",
  "time": "19:00",
  "guests": 4,
  "table": "t12",
  "specialRequest": "Window seat if possible"
}

### 8. Maria books the SAME slot again (expect 409: one booking per slot)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{mariaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Maria Santos",
  "customerEmail": "maria.santos@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09171234567",
  "date": "2026-10-15",
  "time": "19:00",
  "guests": 2
}

### 9. Liza books the same slot (expect 201: she gets Table 6, the next free one)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{lizaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Liza Ramos",
  "customerEmail": "liza.ramos@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09061234567",
  "date": "2026-10-15",
  "time": "19:00",
  "guests": 4
}

### 10. STAFF phone booking, 10 guests, no table chosen (expect 201: Table 12, customer null)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Ernesto Lim",
  "customerEmail": "ernesto.lim@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09271112222",
  "date": "2026-10-15",
  "time": "19:00",
  "guests": 10,
  "specialRequest": "Company dinner"
}

### 11. Slots for Oct 15, 10 guests (expect 19:00 → available false, "Fully booked")
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/slots?date=2026-10-15&guests=10

### 12. Another 10-guest booking at 19:00 (expect 409: no tables available)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Grace Tan",
  "customerEmail": "grace.tan@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09281113333",
  "date": "2026-10-15",
  "time": "19:00",
  "guests": 10
}

### 13. STAFF chooses a specific table that is taken: Table 5 at 19:00 (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Grace Tan",
  "customerEmail": "grace.tan@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09281113333",
  "date": "2026-10-15",
  "time": "19:00",
  "guests": 4,
  "table": "t5"
}


### ===== MY RESERVATIONS + OWNERSHIP =====

### 14. Maria's reservations (expect count 3: r1, r7, and the new one from #7)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/my
Authorization: Bearer {{mariaToken}}

### 15. Liza's reservations (expect count 1)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/my
Authorization: Bearer {{lizaToken}}

### 16. Staff tries /my (expect 403: customers only)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/my
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### 17. Liza tries to VIEW Maria's reservation r1 (expect 403)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/r1
Authorization: Bearer {{lizaToken}}

### 18. Liza tries to CANCEL Maria's reservation r1 (expect 403)
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/r1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{lizaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Not mine"
}

### 19. Maria views her own r1 (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/r1
Authorization: Bearer {{mariaToken}}

### 20. Maria cancels her own r1 (expect 200, cancelledBy "customer")
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/r1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{mariaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Change of plans"
}

### 21. Staff can view ANY reservation (expect 200, status "Cancelled")
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/r1
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
